    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72380.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Let's see. I was 32 when I became a dad and, uh, you know, it changed, it changed my life in a big way. I mean, I always say that getting married is definitely a game changer, but then having kids Really completely totally changes your life. I mean because the kid then becomes everything that your life revolves around and the early days obviously it literally I mean you know the your sleep schedule eating schedule everything revolves around the baby. But then I think for me that as you as you're in my case my boy my first child was boy begins to grow. You really begin to see the world through his eyes and you start thinking about everything that you're doing out the world about well how does this affect my son and what will this mean for him and what will the decisions I make now mean in the future so it kind of for me at least and I think also for my wife for us is a couple really reoriented our view of the world in life.",
