  {
    "episode_id": 72380,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72380.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "yeah that's a serious problems one i encounter every day and and i i think people i mean pretty much every american does when you have a monopoly is these companies do they really don't leave you any alternatives you know i mean social media up to face book face book has no peer competitors same thing with of course you to same thing with google same thing with instagram and Of course, Google owns YouTube and Facebook owns Instagram, so it's really, really consolidated. I mean, what I try to do is, I try to live as much of my life off of these platforms and off of technologies I can. And from my family, what we decided with our kids is to try to live as much of our lives as a family off of these platforms and off of social media, to help our kids cultivate real relationships with other kids to get together and actually play together, not just be chatting online together. And we try to do that with other families it's kind of cool to find other families who share a similar viewpoint and say hey let's try to raise our kids together and let's kind of band together and be a bulwark if you like against a text a desire to to colonize everything that they touch.",
