  {
    "episode_id": 72380,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72380.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Well you know that the thing is with what we're about most with that kind of thing and the people coming to our house and all that sort of thing is really what is my kids i mean i worry about the effect on because they are so young i mean i get my oldest is eight and and and our newest is practically newborn she's six months old so i worry about the effect on them but you know i mean so far we've been very blessed that the kids have not encountered any of that and my wife i just have to give her tremendous credit i mean she is she's as tough as nails. And when we had protesters come to our house and try to shout her down, they actually, I wasn't there when they came to the house. It was at night. She was there alone with the baby and she went out and confronted them. So get out of here. Josh isn't here. And so she has been extraordinarily strong, extraordinarily tough and together. We've tried to put up a shelter around our kids so that they can have a life where they feel, first of all, their home environment feels stable. where they feel like it's safe and where they're just allowed to be kids you know can have a normal life go out play play some sports uh... you know taste of bugs and do some experiments like have a have a fun time and that's what being a kid should be about it and i think because of her toughness and uh... and in doing it together we've been able to give that to my kids but listen that won't always be true my kids i know will inevitably encounter just some of the divisiveness and the shouting and the rage that we see in our culture today. And I hope when that does happen that that will be a moment where I can say to him, hey, this is part of what you encounter in life as you grow up to be an adult, as you grow to be a man, as you grow to be a father, you're going to encounter adversity, you're going to encounter opposition. And you've got to make a choice about how you're going to respond to that and how you're going to push through that. And so I hope that that will be an experience that ultimately when it happens will be a good one for them in that way.",
