  {
    "episode_id": 72380,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72380.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, well the book initially the first publisher of the book tried to cancel it and so back in January the publisher that actually it signed me to contract to write the thing and then tried to cancel it and and keep it from being published so you know that was a hurdle right out of the gate but fortunately was able to find another publisher and bring this thing to publication now people can get it for themselves and you know there's been of course lots of criticism my critics want to come out and and dump on me dump on the book but you know hey that's i mean that's life right i mean that's part of it and you've got it you've got to deal with that criticism deal with that adversity that's part of my job you know this is again to get back to my kids something i hope that i can show my kids by example and then you know one day demonstrate to them as they get older we're able to talk about it that you're going to have critics in life you're going to have adversity you're going to have opponents you can control that is you can control how you respond to it and you can you are responsible for the choices you make and how you respond to those things and it's an opportunity to learn. It's an opportunity to grow. It's an opportunity to get stronger and to push forward. So that's what we're trying to do.",
