    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "I was in the delivery room which was awesome i was able to do that you know mask up and so forth but hey that's small price to pay to be able to be there with my wife and to see my baby daughter born and my wife i was able to go to her appointments i was not able to go with her that was a change you know i couldn't go into all of the appointments leading up to the delivery i remember actually get turned away at one of the early appointments of the hospital i just had thought about you know i'm going and they were like well where are you going and i said well I'm here with my wife for the appointment they're like no you're not you're going to go back to the car and she's going to go to the appointment but we can't have too many people in the building so you know that is what it is I think actually though in these in these first six months you know we've been able to spend so much time together as a family and that's been awesome. So we have we've done very little travel, you know, and the baby really couldn't travel much anyway until now. So that's it. I've been doing a lot less travel than usual because of COVID. So we've really been able to spend that time together as a family. I just tell you, having the six-month-old within two older kids and eight-year-old and six-year-old, that has been tremendous fun watching them react to the baby, watching them learn to become big brothers. It's been awesome.",
