  {
    "episode_id": 72380,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72380.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, well, when we had our third, all the ones were five and four. That first year of having three kids felt like one long day. I mean, it was definitely the most challenging for us going from two to three, then three to four was kind of like a piece of cake, you know, after that. So I know what that's about. And then what does your, what does your bedtime routine look like with your six month old? You a book reader, a lullaby guy, a storyteller. How do you kind of work bedtime?",
