  {
    "episode_id": 72380,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72380.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, very cool. And honestly here, Senator, I think the quarantine has been the silver lining of it has been that a lot of families have had the time to spend together, whereas the dad or mom isn't constantly on the road. So I kind of pray that, you know, that's strengthened our families right there. And maybe that could be like a little bit of the byproduct that's come out of this whole quarantine thing. I mean, with the biggest part of our day is sitting down together as a family every night, praying together, eating dinner together. And it's usually my favorite part of the day. So I hope that that piece could be like the silver lining of the pandemic.",
