  {
    "episode_id": 72380,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72380.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "Well, I just hope to be able to keep representing the people in my state to keep doing the best job that I can possibly do. I say to my kids that, you know, my job is to wake up every morning and is to go do my best. is to do with a clear conscience and I say to them, you know, it's a tremendous privilege to get to serve. I hope that my boys and my daughter will want to grow up and to serve other people in some capacity and any capacity. I think we're all called to do that. This is something I talk to my kids about literally every night telling them to think about, listen, how can we think about serving others? How can we think about helping other people? So I want to try to keep doing that in my life in the area where I'm called, but then also helping my kids grow up to embrace that ethic too. and to find that calling for their own lives. I just have to tell you that, you know, for me as I look forward, the things that really excite me is I'm excited about being a father and I'm excited about seeing my kids grow. My boys and my daughter about living each stage of life with them. And for me, the first and most important calling I have in life is as a husband and as a father and everything else grows out of that.",
